                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "93c6288c-a26a-4767-be1a-6ee5bd72c165",
                        "source_entry_id": "9cbe0234-db00-3454-9830-8b978d266bbb",
                        "source_sense_id": "38346330-82fa-3741-a96b-e14869621c9c",
                        "target_lang_word": "dart",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dart",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "019e0893-70a0-3ccb-a472-857b91e7f7a7",
                                        "entry_id": "74429214-4309-3fe8-9519-2878b1b387de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pointed missile weapon, intended to be thrown by the hand; for example, a short lance or javelin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1382a039-d8a2-4e12-b19d-e255aafebc40",
                                                "sense_id": "019e0893-70a0-3ccb-a472-857b91e7f7a7",
                                                "text": "Then said Joab, I may not tarry thus with thee. And he took three darts in his hand, and thrust them through the heart of Absalom, while he was yet alive in the midst of the oak."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "164e1f0d-00f6-32b5-8275-6657094836cb",
                                        "entry_id": "74429214-4309-3fe8-9519-2878b1b387de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any sharp-pointed missile weapon, such as an arrow."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e08cdd2c-8529-32bf-b07f-592026fa3462",
                                        "entry_id": "74429214-4309-3fe8-9519-2878b1b387de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything resembling such a missile; something that pierces or wounds like such a weapon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16f66d08-d23a-4b9d-8036-4e6d895cdc50",
                                                "sense_id": "e08cdd2c-8529-32bf-b07f-592026fa3462",
                                                "text": "The artful inquiry, whose venom′d dart / Scarce wounds the hearing while it stabs the heart."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66264e99-c1cb-370a-bdd1-9d9f0ef30d60",
                                        "entry_id": "74429214-4309-3fe8-9519-2878b1b387de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small object with a pointed tip at one end and feathers at the other, which is thrown at a target in the game of darts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c741aa1-a1f8-3517-95b7-edc0e9b92548",
                                        "entry_id": "74429214-4309-3fe8-9519-2878b1b387de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cigarette."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "Canada",
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aec91aed-2b64-438f-b346-302250286ab7",
                                                "sense_id": "7c741aa1-a1f8-3517-95b7-edc0e9b92548",
                                                "text": "2017, April 18, Craig Little, The Guardian, Hawthorn are not the only ones finding that things can get worse\nThe Tigers will also face Jesse Hogan, still smarting from missing a couple of games but not life inside the AFL bubble, where you can’t even light up a dart at a music festival without someone filming it and sending it to the six o’clock news."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76a2cf67-68ba-3463-9944-86ccaf11915d",
                                        "entry_id": "74429214-4309-3fe8-9519-2878b1b387de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dart-shaped target towed behind an aircraft to train shooters."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de35339e-0564-48cd-a885-69f89b7a44d2",
                                                "sense_id": "76a2cf67-68ba-3463-9944-86ccaf11915d",
                                                "text": "Fighter aircraft also use restricted areas for target shooting at darts towed 1500 feet behind another aircraft."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bfb5d719-97ac-3b15-9f7c-403120d2f38f",
                                        "entry_id": "74429214-4309-3fe8-9519-2878b1b387de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A plan or scheme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0fcc0aa-0410-49b1-9782-527d164baf99",
                                                "sense_id": "bfb5d719-97ac-3b15-9f7c-403120d2f38f",
                                                "text": "Trucking′s my dart too."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa21ca11-0d52-3ca4-ba3f-89787852dc27",
                                        "entry_id": "74429214-4309-3fe8-9519-2878b1b387de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sudden or fast movement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d0ddcbc-f001-4b40-b28e-7bb270bb0029",
                                                "sense_id": "aa21ca11-0d52-3ca4-ba3f-89787852dc27",
                                                "text": "Soon as I felt the floor tremor I made a dart for the door."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe2e25a2-857a-4b68-bedf-42d5ddd377fd",
                                                "sense_id": "aa21ca11-0d52-3ca4-ba3f-89787852dc27",
                                                "text": "Six minutes later Cueto went over for his second try after the recalled Mike Tindall found him with a perfectly-timed pass, before Ashton went on another dart, this time down his opposite wing, only for his speculative pass inside to be ruled forward."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d98f76fa-813c-3b9c-9bc1-04d4edebaaac",
                                        "entry_id": "74429214-4309-3fe8-9519-2878b1b387de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fold that is stitched on a garment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd06567d-c806-467f-a3ff-6348ffad729d",
                                                "sense_id": "d98f76fa-813c-3b9c-9bc1-04d4edebaaac",
                                                "text": "Somehow she managed, with a cinched waist here and a few darts there, to look like a Hollywood star."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e653c18f-05f8-3c9f-a984-0934ac2d1c28",
                                        "entry_id": "74429214-4309-3fe8-9519-2878b1b387de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dace (fish) (Leuciscus leuciscus)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f3574ee0-0855-3da8-9912-95bf39431729",
                                        "entry_id": "74429214-4309-3fe8-9519-2878b1b387de",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various species of hesperiid butterfly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dart",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d25117cf-4b13-3e89-9a96-d195055d99b9",
                                        "entry_id": "62e36cc4-dbb9-306f-8061-e475989ea3d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To throw with a sudden effort or thrust; to hurl or launch."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "647cb3e6-5d01-327a-91b3-2ce78a78a1c0",
                                        "entry_id": "62e36cc4-dbb9-306f-8061-e475989ea3d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To send forth suddenly or rapidly; to emit; to shoot."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec58841e-b72a-4648-837c-bda56a724463",
                                                "sense_id": "647cb3e6-5d01-327a-91b3-2ce78a78a1c0",
                                                "text": "As the sun darted forth his beams, she darted a meaningful glance at me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a7fe905-2844-4428-903f-362e7202941b",
                                                "sense_id": "647cb3e6-5d01-327a-91b3-2ce78a78a1c0",
                                                "text": "Pan came, and ask'd, what magic caus'd my ſmart, / Or what ill eyes malignant glances dart?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb2f8137-cdbf-4aea-901a-b98d714436d2",
                                                "sense_id": "647cb3e6-5d01-327a-91b3-2ce78a78a1c0",
                                                "text": "Yossarian responded to the thought by slipping away stealthily from the police and almost tripped over the feet of a burly woman of forty hastening across the intersection guiltily, darting furtive, vindictive glances behind her toward a woman of eighty with thick, bandaged ankles doddering after her in a losing pursuit."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1bd26794-4bd1-3328-8a44-bbee7f6fae96",
                                        "entry_id": "62e36cc4-dbb9-306f-8061-e475989ea3d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To shoot with a dart, especially a tranquilizer dart."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b46abf2-5259-41ce-9346-7e9f8e32cf16",
                                                "sense_id": "1bd26794-4bd1-3328-8a44-bbee7f6fae96",
                                                "text": "They had to dart the animal to get close enough to help"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b4a1e48-a35e-304e-845f-b2e50864185d",
                                        "entry_id": "62e36cc4-dbb9-306f-8061-e475989ea3d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fly or pass swiftly, like a dart; to move rapidly in one direction; to shoot out quickly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17ce96be-aebd-4086-946f-f3bfc124b82e",
                                                "sense_id": "9b4a1e48-a35e-304e-845f-b2e50864185d",
                                                "text": "The flying man darted eastward."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a2728880-044b-360d-bc5d-945d43af3e12",
                                        "entry_id": "62e36cc4-dbb9-306f-8061-e475989ea3d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To start and run with speed; to shoot rapidly along."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0befc68f-c9cf-4c1d-9683-34a63d8d8b57",
                                                "sense_id": "a2728880-044b-360d-bc5d-945d43af3e12",
                                                "text": "The deer darted from the thicket."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c3d7d1d-fc10-4323-8c25-9cb78cb51f6d",
                                                "sense_id": "a2728880-044b-360d-bc5d-945d43af3e12",
                                                "text": "The fish darted under a stone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6249ded-d8f9-4242-814d-4a6086f9740a",
                                                "sense_id": "a2728880-044b-360d-bc5d-945d43af3e12",
                                                "text": "By half-time, it was almost a surprise that the away side had restricted themselves to only one more goal. Messi, again, was prominently involved, darting past Fernando and then Zabaleta."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad04553c-24b2-41d1-b19a-7350a4a717c8",
                                                "sense_id": "a2728880-044b-360d-bc5d-945d43af3e12",
                                                "text": "The impressive Frenchman drove forward with purpose down the right before cutting infield and darting in between Vassiriki Diaby and Koscielny."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9e4264a1-fcba-460c-9cf9-01e888dd466c",
                        "source_entry_id": "9cbe0234-db00-3454-9830-8b978d266bbb",
                        "source_sense_id": "38346330-82fa-3741-a96b-e14869621c9c",
                        "target_lang_word": "javelin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "javelin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1109e4c4-82a6-38de-ab97-098ef88c99bb",
                                        "entry_id": "773adb19-3873-33ee-ac4d-5f3e83cb7bb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A light spear thrown with the hand and used as a weapon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa264059-45e3-43ee-8c09-ad7b145c3fd3",
                                                "sense_id": "1109e4c4-82a6-38de-ab97-098ef88c99bb",
                                                "text": "And when Phinehas the sonne of Eleazar, the sonne of Aaron the Priest saw it, hee rose vp from amongst the Congregation, and tooke a iauelin in his hand. And he went after the man of Israel into the tent, and thrust both of them thorow, the man of Israel, and the woman, thorow her belly: So the plague was stayed from the children of Israel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d586b22b-e91a-4f6c-a8cc-bfb4244f31c3",
                                                "sense_id": "1109e4c4-82a6-38de-ab97-098ef88c99bb",
                                                "text": "Flies the javelin swifter to its mark, / Launched by the vigour of a Roman arm?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5fe8993-ea4c-42c6-a406-8a8d0b414d1d",
                                                "sense_id": "1109e4c4-82a6-38de-ab97-098ef88c99bb",
                                                "text": "With what apprehensions we proceeded, ignorant at what moment we might be greeted by the javelin of some ambushed savage!",
                                                "translation": "Typee",
                                                "english": "Typee"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5580bb05-d9c3-4abe-99cc-104d0f8b37f8",
                                                "sense_id": "1109e4c4-82a6-38de-ab97-098ef88c99bb",
                                                "text": "As a lion or wild boar turns fiercely on the dogs and men that attack him, while these form a solid wall and shower their javelins as they face him—his courage is all undaunted, but his high spirit will be the death of him;[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ba1c9e7-3b34-4179-b962-fc9cca6e496b",
                                                "sense_id": "1109e4c4-82a6-38de-ab97-098ef88c99bb",
                                                "text": "Searching through snow / For the javelin I had not / Meant to throw right at you / For if it had hit its mark / There’d be blood in the place / Where you stood"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd8598a4-2016-31bb-8038-84dde17fb41d",
                                        "entry_id": "773adb19-3873-33ee-ac4d-5f3e83cb7bb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A metal-tipped spear thrown for distance in an athletic field event."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "547c9f7d-beca-3fac-b1ea-3e094ca1d4cf",
                                        "entry_id": "773adb19-3873-33ee-ac4d-5f3e83cb7bb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A javelinfish (Coelorinchus australis)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "javelin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ee96eba-97b0-3c30-8fec-a76eb66039cd",
                                        "entry_id": "884093df-b694-33f8-9099-cad0a0201796",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To pierce with a javelin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b7499db-e9de-4e81-bdec-2026fbd56da4",
                                                "sense_id": "6ee96eba-97b0-3c30-8fec-a76eb66039cd",
                                                "text": "Furrowing a giant oak, and javelining / With darted spikes and splinters of the wood"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bd063a0-69e1-40fc-9091-d3548a095a17",
                                                "sense_id": "6ee96eba-97b0-3c30-8fec-a76eb66039cd",
                                                "text": "Eventually ostriches arrived and with arrows I shot them in the burning arena with arrows tipped with small bronze crescents Saw flies buzz at the array of javelinned lions Saw the looks on faces crookedly aghast when before them I hoisted a hacked off ostrich head and wagged my own and grinned"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "00745b07-a975-309a-82a7-da993641dff9",
                                        "entry_id": "884093df-b694-33f8-9099-cad0a0201796",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To throw like a javelin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7cefbb8c-d335-472d-a0b0-d658c606555b",
                                                "sense_id": "00745b07-a975-309a-82a7-da993641dff9",
                                                "text": "He will have questions of all sorts javelined at him from the benches on both sides, from above the gangway and from below it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97177fe7-baf2-41f3-92b5-b670db35215a",
                                                "sense_id": "00745b07-a975-309a-82a7-da993641dff9",
                                                "text": "There is a thing no man may name; / It comes like beauty, goes like flame. / It haunts dim labyrinths of time / And enters every poet’s rhyme. / Its cry is heard upon the wind / When it is high and javelinned, / And on still nights its steps are heard, / Soft as the footfalls of a bird."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64766eb6-af4d-496f-bd8b-80b0009c7aa8",
                                                "sense_id": "00745b07-a975-309a-82a7-da993641dff9",
                                                "text": "The year the tornado swept through, it scattered the debris of two garages and their contents outward for hundreds of yards. An 8-foot 2-by-4 was javelinned through my bedroom wall; its blunt end stared at me just three feet short of my bed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3c54323-fc89-43bf-99a1-0636aea23ea5",
                                                "sense_id": "00745b07-a975-309a-82a7-da993641dff9",
                                                "text": "good morning city. another day of digging. wrapping. numbering. dnaing. […] of reciting a poem by li po. about forever. about wrapping forever into a ball. about wrapping forever into a ball and javelinning it out to sea. the beautiful beautiful sea."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "066505be-7e00-4f66-9602-6ede3fe725d8",
                                                "sense_id": "00745b07-a975-309a-82a7-da993641dff9",
                                                "text": "To retrieve the mophead she would have to immerse her hand into the bucket’s stagnant grey water and kitchen-floor debris. At the thought of doing so, she javelinned the mop handle onto the floor, the speed and violence of which action, afterward, made her feel deranged."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "85387e75-47e8-3dfe-8849-05c3b2f178b8",
                                        "entry_id": "884093df-b694-33f8-9099-cad0a0201796",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fall like a javelin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7cf8591c-fdf1-404b-b8eb-29df0b1026ff",
                                                "sense_id": "85387e75-47e8-3dfe-8849-05c3b2f178b8",
                                                "text": "For answer the ship righted as she rolled upon another great swell, leaned as far the other side, and crashed, bows first, into a cleft rock under water which held her as in a vise while her jib boom flew up in splinters, and her foretopgallant and royal mast, with yards and gear and sails, tore loose aloft and javelined down until brought up short by the involved rigging."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80067603-6d37-4410-9403-d2b9bce2f306",
                                                "sense_id": "85387e75-47e8-3dfe-8849-05c3b2f178b8",
                                                "text": "The ants broke loose and attacked. In an attempt to beat them off, Ejeka lost grip of his whip which javelinned earthward."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b0731e6-ba6c-42a1-88e9-0b2b1122e904",
                                                "sense_id": "85387e75-47e8-3dfe-8849-05c3b2f178b8",
                                                "text": "Jagged bolts of lightning javelined down from the sky, attempting to skewer him with their electrical touch."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa58fd68-f13d-4722-a685-5e7818a50bd8",
                                                "sense_id": "85387e75-47e8-3dfe-8849-05c3b2f178b8",
                                                "text": "One man dropped his rifle from high up and it javelined down, with the muzzle burying itself deep in the ground."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
